  "raw_label": "postponed_or_procedural",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Isha Foundation vs S. Kamaraj on 3 October, 2024 1 Item No.801 Court No.1 Sect S U P R E M E C O U R T O F I N D I A Record Of Proceedings Special Leave Petition (Criminal) Diary No(s). 45881/2024 (Arising out of impugned final judgment and order dated 30-09-2024 in Sc-Atr No. 2487/2024 passed by the High Court Of Judicature At Madras At Chennai) Isha Foundation Peti Versus S. Kamaraj & Ors. Resp Date : 03-10-2024 This petition was called on for hearing today. Coram : Hon'Ble The Chief Justice Hon'Ble Mr. Justice J.B. Pardiwala Hon'Ble Mr. Justice Manoj Misra For Petitioner(s) Mr Mukul Rohatgi, Sr. Adv.",
    "facts": "1 A habeas corpus petition was filed under Article 226 of the Constitution by the first respondent, seeking the production of his daughters - Geeta Kamraj and Lata Kamraj - who, he alleged, were held captive inside the premises of Isha Foundation at Coimbatore. After noticing the submissions of counsel for the petitioner to the effect that several other persons were staying at the Ashram of Isha Foundation in Coimbatore out of compulsion, the High Court issued a general direction ordering that with reference to the said allegations, Coimbatore Rural Police having jurisdiction shall conduct an enquiry and file a status report before this Court. Isha Foundation vs S. Kamaraj on 3 October, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/198279101/ 1 3 Both the individuals stated that (i) they are residing at the Ashram voluntarily and without any coercion; (ii) they are free to travel outside the Ashram which they have done from time to time; (iii) one of the individuals has participated in a marathon run extending to about 10 kilometers in Hyderabad; and (iv) their parents visit the Ashram periodically to meet them.",
    "arguments": "4 Mr Siddharth Luthra, senior counsel has appeared in these proceedings on behalf of the State of Tamil Nadu and its officers - Respondent Nos 2, 3 and 4 and states that the Police team which conducted the enquiry in pursuance of the impugned order of the High Court was accompanied by the: (i) District Child Welfare Committee headed by its Chairperson; (ii) District Child Protection Officer and team; (iii) District Social Welfare Officer; (iv) Joint Director, Health; (v) Two Psychiatrist; and (vi) Food Safety Officer."
  },
